WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.575
Welcome. This is your ten-day listening plan.

2
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:07.553
The goal is that your child hears the sounds inside a short word. Like this.

3
00:00:07.953 --> 00:00:08.890
The word is sun.

4
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.535
This video tells you what the plan is, what to expect, and how to use it.

5
00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:22.185
This plan is for a child who cannot yet say how a word starts.

6
00:00:22.635 --> 00:00:24.047
Or who cannot rhyme yet.

7
00:00:24.497 --> 00:00:27.521
Or who cannot pull a short word apart into its sounds.

8
00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:34.324
That is common at four and five. Nobody hears the separate sounds in a word until someone shows them.

9
00:00:34.774 --> 00:00:40.369
It comes before letters. A child who cannot hear the sounds has nothing to match a letter to.

10
00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:45.673
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

11
00:00:46.123 --> 00:00:51.268
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

12
00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:57.573
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. You hear every sound done right before you say it.

13
00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:03.001
The pages are pictures. There is almost nothing to read. This plan is for the ears.

14
00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:09.417
Now, what to expect. The start of a word is the easiest part to hear. So that comes first.

15
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:11.791
Then the end of a word, and rhymes.

16
00:01:12.241 --> 00:01:18.707
Then your child pushes sounds together into a word, and pulls a word apart. The middle sound comes last.

17
00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:23.793
Some days need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

18
00:01:24.243 --> 00:01:31.406
This plan is practice in the right order. It is not a promise. On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

19
00:01:32.206 --> 00:01:38.703
One thing matters more than anything else. Say the sound, not the name of the letter. And keep it short and clean.

20
00:01:39.153 --> 00:01:40.534
This is how map starts.

21
00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.978
It is a hum. Nothing is added on the end.

22
00:01:45.778 --> 00:01:52.264
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

23
00:01:52.714 --> 00:01:57.283
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

24
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:03.564
The first step is always the same. Say the name of every picture, and your child says it after you.

25
00:02:04.014 --> 00:02:07.162
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

26
00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:12.711
Then your child does job two alone, and checks it against the answers printed upside down.

27
00:02:13.161 --> 00:02:18.164
On days seven and eight there is a sound track for your child. You press play and step away.

28
00:02:18.964 --> 00:02:24.957
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and three counters. Coins, beans or buttons will do.

29
00:02:25.407 --> 00:02:32.291
If your child often does not seem to hear well, ask the doctor about a hearing check. This plan cannot tell you that.

30
00:02:32.741 --> 00:02:37.829
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
